export anchor WarehouseLogisticsStyle:
    number: 133
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Warehouse logistics
    idea: The dashboard as a warehouse dispatch board, with aisle signs for navigation, numbers on hazard striped counters, each project a shipping label with a bin location, a barcode and cartons loaded, and the daily chart as a row of conveyor belts.
    base: light
    palette:
        concrete: #e9e8e3, the floor, with a faint 120px grid
        labelWhite: #ffffff, labels, panels and fields
        black: #111111, text, 2 to 3px borders, aisle signs and barcodes
        steel: #4f4f4b, small codes and meta
        forkliftYellow: #f5c400, the top band, bins, the current aisle and the focus halo, never text on light
        kraft: #c89b62, cartons and the label offset shadow, edged #8a6233
        rule: #b9b8b0, table rules
        onTrack: #17663a, the ticked box
        atRisk: #8a4b00, the triangle
        behind: #b3121b, the crossed octagon, the overdue tag and the late label shadow
    type:
        Labels and text use Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue
        Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial, sans-serif, with bold caps
        for labels. Codes and numbers use OCR A Std, OCR A Extended,
        ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is
        40px 700 at 1.05, counters 46px 700 mono, label names 24px 700,
        pallet codes 13px mono tracked 0.2em, body 15px at 1.45, field
        labels such as SHIP TO and BIN 11px mono.
    layout:
        A forklift yellow top band with a kraft carton logo, the caps brand
        with DC-01 DISPATCH BOARD in mono, a boxed search, a black New
        project button with yellow text, a square bell and a black MO badge
        with the name, edged below by a black and yellow hazard stripe. The
        nav is six black aisle signs hanging on short posts, each with a
        yellow square letter A to F and the label, the current Home sign
        yellow with a black letter. The greeting sits on a white dock door
        panel tagged DOOR 01 with the date in mono, and a red luggage tag
        shape says 4 TASKS ARE OVERDUE. Four counters with a hazard striped
        top hold the numbers in mono with bin codes K-01 to K-04, the overdue
        counter striped red and white. Outbound projects shows six shipping
        labels three across, each with a 3px black border and a hard kraft
        offset shadow, red for the late one. A label has a SHIP TO team cell
        and a yellow BIN cell, the project name, a row of ten carton boxes
        filled by tens of percent with the percent, cartons done of total
        and the due date, a barcode with a pallet code such as BW-WR-1114,
        and a bordered status stamp. Below, Throughput draws each day as a
        conveyor belt with carton segments, one per task, under black week
        headers with totals, beside a Dock log table with mono times. Below
        1100px labels go two across and aisles three, below 600px everything
        stacks and aisles go two across.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 20px between counters and labels and 24px between panels.
    density: Busy but scannable, like a dispatch board. Three labels across with codes everywhere.
    corners: Square. The overdue tag has a cut luggage tag point.
    borders: 3px black on labels with 3px divider rows, 2px on everything else, hazard stripes on top edges.
    shadows: A hard 6px kraft offset under each label, red when the project is behind. No blur.
    icons:
        Bold filled signs at 18px inside a bordered stamp with the caps word,
        a ticked box for ON TRACK, a triangle with a bar for AT RISK and a
        crossed octagon for BEHIND, plus a carton logo.
    focus: A 3px black outline offset 2px inside a 6px forklift yellow halo.
    tone: Floor operations, such as Outbound projects, Ship to, Bin, Cartons, Throughput and Dock log.
